{"url":"http://www.time-travellers.org/oftpd/","name":"oftpd page","note":"oftpd is designed to be as secure as an anonymous FTP server can possibly be. It runs as non-root for most of the time, and uses the Unix chroot() command to hide most of the systems directories from external users - they cannot change into them even if the server is totally compromised! It contains its own directory change code, so that it can run efficiently as a threaded server, and its own directory listing code (most FTP servers execute the system \"ls\" command to list files).\n","tags":"opera"}
