{"url":"http://handhelds.org/moin/moin.cgi/Ipkg","name":"Ipkg - Handhelds.org MoinMoin Wiki","note":"ipkg - the Itsy Package Management SystemiPKG is a very lightweight package management system. It was designed for Linux installations with severe storage limitations such as handheld computers. iPKG is more than just an embedded Linux flash image builder, (although it does that fairly well). It also allows for dynamic installation/removal of packages on a running system. note: see BuildingIpkgs for details on creating your own ipkg files. iPKG is itsy in several ways: The control programs themselves are small, (currently about 13kB) The installed meta-data tries to be only what is absolutely essential, (currently about 38kB for a 16MB compressed flash iPAQ distribution) The available packages are small. (The idea is that the package tree should be as fine-grain as possible. Much of this still needs some work)\n","tags":"opera"}
