{"url":"https://code.google.com/p/cefpython/","name":"None","note":"CEF Python is an open source project founded by Czarek Tomczak in 2012 to provide python bindings for the Chromium Embedded Framework (in short CEF), a web browser control based on Google Chrome. With CEF you can implement a HTML 5 based GUI in a desktop application or provide browser capabilities to an application, see the growing list of applications using CEF on the wikipedia page. Bindings to CEF are possible thanks to Cython which allows to use c++ libraries directly in Python.\n","tags":"python,html5,desktop"}
{"url":"https://ksdaemon.github.io/wiola/","name":"Wiola by KSDaemon","note":"Wiola implements WAMP v2 router specification on top of OpenResty web app server, which is actually nginx plus a bunch of 3rd party modules, such as lua-nginx-module, lua-resty-websocket, lua-resty-redis, lua-resty-libcjson and so on. wiola supports next WAMP roles and features: broker: advanced profile with features: subscriber blackwhite listing publisher exclusion publisher identification dealer: advanced profile with features: callee blackwhite listing caller exclusion caller identification progressive call results Wiola supports JSON and msgpack serializers. From v0.3.1 Wiola also supports lightweight POST event publishing. See processPostData method and post-handler.lua for details.\n","tags":"lua,opensource,nginx,openresty,websocket,tweetthis"}
