{"url":"http://mrsync.sourceforge.net/","name":"SourceForge.net mrsync (multicast remote sync) - Project Web Hosting - Open Source Software","note":"SourceForge presents the mrsync (multicast remote sync) project. mrsync (multicast remote sync) is an open source application. SourceForge provides the world's largest selection of Open Source Software. mrsync a tool to transfer files from a master to many remote machines in LAN using Unix socket's multicast. It dynamically adjusts its speed of transfering to ease on the network and to leave no one behind. 4 hours for 140GB to 100 targets in 1Gbit LANAbout this project: This is the mrsync (multicast remote sync) project (\"mrsync\") This project was registered on SourceForge.net on May 17, 2006, and is described by the project team as follows: mrsync a tool to transfer files from a master to many remote machines in LAN using Unix socket's multicast. It dynamically adjusts its speed of transfering to ease on the network and to leave no one behind. 4 hours for 140GB to 100 targets in 1Gbit LAN About SourceForge.net: SourceForge.net is the world's largest provider of hosting for Open Sour...\n","tags":"opera"}
