{"url":"http://code.google.com/p/osd-lyrics/","name":"osd-lyrics - Project Hosting on Google Code","note":"OSD Lyrics is inspired by lrcdis. With OSD Lyrics, you can enjoy an OSD lyrics show with various media players in Linux. Note: Due to a recent bug, if you succeed in searching lyrics but fail in downloading, please make the directory \"~/.lyrics\" Compatible Media PlayersTo get a full list of supported functions of each player, see list of compatible players Amarok 2.0 and 1.4 (1.4 are disabled by default, use --enable-amarok1 to compile) Audacious Banshee Exaile (Both 0.2 and 0.3) MOC 2.5 (High CPU Usage) Quod Libet new! MPD Rhythmbox Songbird (with MPRIS extension installed) XMMS2 Download LyricsOSD Lyrics can download lyrics from following web sites: Sogou Qianqian You can switch the download engine in preference dialog. Have Trouble?Read our FAQ Post to our discussion group or send a mail to osd-lyrics@googlegroups.com. You can also fire an issue. Get InvolvedIf you would like to translate OSD Lyrics to other languagues, please visit our translation site If there is any feature req...\n","tags":"opera"}
