{"url":"http://home.gna.org/vncssld/","name":"vncssld - The VNC SSL repeater for UNIX","note":"vncssld 是一个 Linux 和 Unix 系统下的 VNC SSL 中继器，你可以用它来透过 VNC SSL 访问你的远程服务器桌面。使用 VNC SSL 中继器的好处是你不需要为你的远程计算机再独立的配置防火墙。This is a VNC SSL repeater for UNIX. You can use it to be able to access your user's desktop using VNC SSL. The advantage of using a repeater is that you don't need to configure your firewall to be able to connect to your user's desktop. Since it is using SSL, It can even work using standard HTTP/HTTPS proxy (like squid or dansguardian). The main advantages of VNCSSLD are: Written in Perl 5, so no buffer overflow should be possible.High security level using standard protocol (SSL is used for https).You don't need to bother about configuring port forwarding on your internet router (for VNC clients and VNC servers).Can run as unprivileged user.Counterparts: It has only be tested on Linux systems. It should work on any UNIX platform supporting Perl 5. It has never been tested under Microsoft Windows and should probably never run under this platform since it is using the POSIX m...\n","tags":"opera"}
