{"url":"http://code.google.com/p/qwit/","name":"qwit - Google Code","note":"Starting from 0.8 release Qwit has a project team! Welcome, Uğur Çetin, kiracatgirl, Valentin Gritsinger, Perry Ismangil! Thanks to soko1, now we have FreeBSD port for Qwit: http://truebsd.org/sokolov/344 Note. Primary Qwit's platform is Linux. Despite this I always compile it for Windows, but now I cannot guarantee that it works good there, so use it on your own risk. This project was started with the purpose of studying Qt4 programming. It could be useful, for example, for KDE users, who need a natively looking client for their systems. And of couse it works in Gnome, Windows and every system that is supported by Qt. Latest version features: depends on Qt4 only; KDE native look; http-proxy support; userpics caching; clickable links in statuses; public, replies, custom user timelines, search; caching messages between sessions; replies, retweets and direct messages support; customizable interface.\n","tags":"opera"}
