{"url":"http://www.wafflegrid.com/","name":"Waffle Grid Project","note":"The simple answer is that a Waffle Grid is a distributed Level 2 Cache for Innodb.  The goal of a Waffle Grid is to allow you to avoid going to disk if at all possible.  In Innodb when a block goes through the LRU, instead of just going away to be reread from disk the next time through, we put that block in Memcached.  Next time that block is needed it can then be pulled out of Memcached instead of being read off of disk.\nWaffle Grid is still in an early phase, but we have made great strides over the the last few months when it comes to stability and performance.  Waffle Grid is release under a GPL license and is available on launchpad.\n","tags":""}
