{"url":"http://rpyc.sourceforge.net/index.html","name":"RPyC","note":"RPyC (IPA: /ɑɹ paɪ siː/, pronounced like are-pie-see), or Remote Python Call, is a transparent python library for symmetrical remote procedure calls, clustering and distributed-computing. RPyC makes use of object-proxying, a technique that employs python’s dynamic nature, to overcome the physical boundaries between processes and computers, so that remote objects can be manipulated as if they were local.\n","tags":"rpc,python,tweetthis"}
