{"url":"http://code.google.com/p/muggles/","name":"muggles - Project Hosting on Google Code","note":"Muggles is an acronym for multiple uplink gateway for GNU/Linux Enterprise Systems. It is a debian-based multiple gateway WAN router. You typically use it to connect a LAN up to the internet via multiple not-100%-reliable dsl uplinks, thereby achieving practically 100% connectivity for an office. The connectivity is logged; machines on the lan can be moved between uplinks; and services like dnsmasq, ntpd and squid on the router improve aspects of networking for the end users. The system adheres to The Debian Way, so you can rely on adding more debian packages as needed without breaking things. It currently (26th Feb 2010) runs with lenny (stable) and squeeze (testing) and is intended to always track debian stable - ie it is meant for production use.\n","tags":""}
