{"url":"http://hippie.oofle.com/","name":"HiPPIE","note":"About HiPPIEHiPPIE, or the Hi-Performance Protocol Identification Engine is a project started by Josh Ballard to provide a new way to do protocol identification in network devices. Built as an extension to the Linux kernel and based on intelligent examination of network packets, it allows other pieces of software to make decisions about those packets based on the information that HiPPIE can provide. Unlike many other identification engines out there whose only method of operation is simple byte- or string-matching, HiPPIE allows for complex algorithms to be applied to packet inspection, plus features session tracking, session prediction, tunnel tracking (more coming soon), and many other advanced features to help facilitate further identification of traffic. Also, unlike most identification systems, HiPPIE's use is not limited to purely that of the packet filtering system, but is built to be plugged into by any system that can pass packets and needs protocol identification.Possbiliti...\n","tags":"opera"}
{"url":"http://www.webpagetest.org/","name":"Pagetest - where web sites go to get FAST!","note":"Speed up the performance of your web pages with an automated analysisPagetest allows you to provide the URL of a webpage to be tested. The test will be conducted from the location specified and you will be provided a waterfall of your page load performance as well as a comparison against an optimization checklist. Please visit the PageTest wiki page for more information. Sample results for AOL.com can be seen here. This tool lets you test web pages that are directly accessible as an URL from the Internet. If you need to test a page inside of a firewall or something more complicated than a web page (an authenticated product like webmail for example) please download the desktop version of PageTest which this is based on.在线测试web\n","tags":"opera"}
