{"url":"http://live.gnome.org/gtk-vnc","name":"gtk-vnc - GNOME Live!","note":"gtk-vnc is a VNC viewer widget for GTK. It is built using coroutines allowing it to be completely asynchronous while remaining single threaded. It provides a core C library, and bindings for Python (PyGTK). The API is still in early stages of development &amp; so until version 1.0 is declared, the API may change. The primary public API is provided by the vncdisplay.h class &amp; should be reasonably free of API churn. The other header files are internal VNC protocol implementation &amp; will very likely change. GTK-VNC supports a number of VNC extensions aimed at improving the user experience, particularly when interacting with virtual machines.\n","tags":"opera"}
