{"url":"http://www.nicotine-plus.org/","name":"Nicotine+","note":"What is Nicotine and Nicotine+?\n\nHyriand's rewrite of  PySoulSeek with a  PyGTK2 GUI is called  Nicotine. \n\n Nicotine+ is an attempt to keep Nicotine working with the latest libraries, kill bugs, keep current with the  Soulseek protocol and add some new features that users want and/or need.\n\nThe main developers are daelstorm, quinox and hedonist.\n","tags":""}
{"url":"https://github.com/doat/geodis","name":"doat/geodis · GitHub","note":"Geodis - a Redis based geo resolving library\nGeodis is a simple and fast python module that allows you to convert IP addresses and latitude/longitude coordinates into geographical locations such as cities, zipcodes and countries.\n\nIt currently supports cities worldwide, and zipcode areas in the US (of course each of these includes higher level data such as country). But it is written in an extensible way, so that adding a new layer of objects and indexing them is very simple.\n\nGeodis is fast, since it uses redis, which as a very fast in memory database, and geohashing to index coordinates.\n\na single thread, signle process python program can resolve about 2000 ips and 3000 lat/lon pairs per second on a regular desktop machine, when the database is fully loaded with IP ranges, zipcodes and all major cities in the world.\n","tags":"ip2location, redis, python, "}
