{"url":"http://blog.jwchat.org/jwchat/","name":"JWChat","note":"Weblog about web based jabber chat clients for easy integration into web communities adding real time presence information and messaging capabilitiesJWChat is a full featured, web-based Jabber™ client. Written using AJAX technology it relies on JavaScript and HTML at the client-side only. It supports basicjabber instant messaging, roster management and groupchats based on theMUC protocol.JWChat is an advanced instant messenger (IM) just like AIM, MSNMessenger, Yahoo! Messenger or ICQ. This means you can manage yourcontacts, communicate with other users in 1:1 chat sessions or join a groupchat room forcollaborative communication. Unlike other IMs you can use this with yourweb browser without having to install any additional software atall. For a list of supported browsers seethe features page.All of your settings, bookmarks and your contact list are stored onthe server side. This means that you have access to your personalizedclient from almost any computer as long as it’s got access ...\n","tags":"opera"}
