{"url":"http://www.askozia.com/pbx/","name":"AskoziaPBX at Askozia","note":"Open Source DevelopmentAskozia®PBX aims to make the power of Asterisk® available to the average user in a slimmed down, embedded PC friendly form.AskoziaPBX is more than another GUI for Asterisk. It is an embedded PBX solution which eases system upgrades, backups and provisioning.Basics:&lt; 15 MB firmware imagedesigned for low-power systemsbased on Asterisk 1.4 and FreeBSD 6.3all system configuration stored in a single XML filePlatforms:generic x86 pc (min. 64MB RAM, 200MHz CPU)PC Engines: wrap, alix1x, alix2x and alix3xSoekris: net48xx, net55xxHerologic: hl4xxFeatures:easily configurable phone and provider accounts for SIP, IAX, ISDN and Analog devicesWireless Access Point functionalityConferencing, Call Groups, Call Parking, TransfersVoicemail via E-MailLocalizations for: Bulgarian, Chinese (simplified / traditional), Danish, Dutch, English (USA / UK), French (FR / CA), German, Greek, Italian, Japanese, Polish, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish, Swedish\n","tags":"opera"}
