{"url":"http://linux-iscsi.sourceforge.net/","name":"Linux-iSCSI Project","note":"Linux-iSCSI Projectdriver and daemon for using iSCSI on LinuxOverviewThe Linux iSCSI driver acts as an iSCSI protocol initiator to transport SCSI requests and responses over an IP network between the client and an iSCSI-enabled target device such as a Cisco SN 5428-2 storage router. The iSCSI protocol is an IETF-defined protocol for IP storage. For more information about the iSCSI protocol, refer to http://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3720.txt.\n","tags":"opera"}
